    tags: ["radio-control-office", "martial-law", "historical", "registration"],
    cross_references: [],
    fullText: "Republic of the Philippines\n                   Department of Transportation and Communications\n                            RADIO CONTROL OFFICE\n                                     Quezon City\n\n                                                     October 12, 1972\n\nMEMORANDUM CIRCULAR\nNO.     5\n\nSUBJECT:       Requiring all persons, companies and corporations, other than\n               authorized radio dealers and manufacturers, possessing unregistered\n               radio transmitters and/or transceivers to register same not later than\n               November 15, 1972 with the Radio Control Office or its Field Officer\n               without penalty.\n\n        Pursuant to Letter of Instruction No. 13-A of the President of the Philippines\ndated September 29, 1972, all persons, companies and corporations, other than authorized\nradio dealers and manufacturers, possessing unregistered radio transmitters and/or\ntransceivers are enjoined to register same without penalty irrespective of source or origin\nwith the Radio Control Office, Department of Public Works, Transportation and\nCommunication, at 86 Quezon Blvd. Extension, Quezon City, or with its Field Offices at\nCebu City, Tolosa, Leyte and Davao City, not later than November 15, 1972.\n\n       Failure to comply with this Circular within the announced deadline will subject\nthose concerned to the provisions of Act 2846, as amended, and the confiscation of said\nunregistered radio transmitters and/or transceivers.\n\n                                     (SGD.) CEFERINO S. CARREON\n                                     Acting Radio Regulation chief",
    sections: [
      { heading: "Registration Requirement", body: "All persons, companies, and corporations other than authorized radio dealers and manufacturers possessing unregistered radio transmitters and/or transceivers, irrespective of source or origin, must register them with the Radio Control Office in Quezon City or its Field Offices in Cebu City, Tolosa (Leyte), and Davao City, not later than November 15, 1972, without penalty." },
      { heading: "Consequence of Non-Compliance", body: "Failure to comply within the announced deadline subjects those concerned to the provisions of Act 3846, as amended, and to confiscation of the unregistered radio transmitters and/or transceivers." }
    ]
