    title: "MC 11-04-2000 - Amendment to Age Qualification for NTC Licensure Examinations",
    shortTitle: "Amended Age Qualification for NTC Licensure Exams",
    type: "regulation",
    category: "Memorandum Circulars",
    status: "active",
    effective_date: "2000-04-14",
    tags: ["gmdss", "radio-operator-certificate", "qualifications"],
    cross_references: ["mc-13-11-91", "mc-09-07-98"],
    fullText: "MEMORANDUM CIRCULAR\nNO. 11-04-2000\n\nSUBJECT:      Amendment to age qualification of an applicant to qualify for the NTC\n              licensure examination as stipulated under items, 1.b 2.2.1 and 2.2.2 of\n              Memorandum Circular Nos. 13-11-91, 09-07-98 and 06-06-98 respectively.\n\nIn compliance with ITU Radio Regulations, Chapter NIX Article 55 and the provisions of\nSection IV/2, Item 2.1, STCW Convention of 1995, the National Telecommunications\nCommission (NTC) pursuant to the powers vested upon it hereby amends the age qualification of\nan applicant to be able to take the GOC, ROC and REC licensure examination, to read as\nfollows;\n\n                             “He must be at least 20 years of age”\n\nWith the above amendment, all other provisions in Memorandum Circular Nos. 13-11-91, 09-07-\n98 and 06-06-98 stands.\n\nQuezon City, Philippines, April 14, 2000.\n\n                              (SGD.) JOSEPH A. SANTIAGO\n                                      Commissioner\n\n(SGD.) NESTOR C. DACANAY                                      (SGD.) AURELIO M. UMALI\n   Deputy Commissioner                                           Deputy Commissioner\n\n                                               1",
    sections: [
      { heading: "Amended Age Requirement", body: "Sets the minimum age qualification for GOC, ROC, and REC licensure examination applicants at 20 years old, with all other provisions of MC Nos. 13-11-91, 09-07-98, and 06-06-98 remaining in force." }
    ]
