    tags: ["radio-training-center", "gmdss", "qualifications"],
    cross_references: [],
    fullText: "Memorandum Circular\nNo. 02-02-2003\n\nSUBJECT       :       Addendum to Memorandum Circular No. 17-12-2002 Re: Rules\n                      and Regulations governing Radio Training Centers (RTC) offering\n                      short-term GMDSS radio communications courses.\n\nPursuant to Act 3846, as amended, E.O. No. 546, Chapter NIX Article 55 of the Radio\nRegulations of International Telecommunications Union (ITU), and Regulations 1/6 and\n1/8 of the 1978 STCW Convention, as amended, the Memorandum Circular No. 17-12-\n2002 dated December 20, 2002 is hereby amended to include a new provision, item “d”\nof Section VI, 6.1, as follows:\n\n              “d” ,   If applicant is not a deck/radio officer or ECE, he/she may be\n                      allowed to attend the training, provided, it shall only be issued a\n                      “Certificate of Attendance” upon completion of the course. The\n                      Certificate of Attendance shall not be considered as a basis for\n                      qualifying in the GOC or ROC examination.\n\nAll other provisions of Memorandum Circular No. 17-12-2002 remains in force.\n\nFeb. 12, 2003 , Quezon City, Philippines\n\nARMI JANE R. BORJE\nCommissioner",
    sections: [
      { heading: "New Provision", body: "An applicant who is not a deck/radio officer or Electronics and Communications Engineer (ECE) may attend RTC training but will only be issued a Certificate of Attendance upon completion, which does not qualify as a basis for taking the GOC or ROC examination. All other provisions of MC 17-12-2002 remain in force." }
    ]
