    tags: ["maritime", "safety-equipment"],
    cross_references: ["mc-04-09-88"],
    fullText: "MEMORANDUM CIRCULAR\nNO. 11-24-88\n\nSUBJECT:      AMENDING MEMORANDUM CIRCULAR NO. 04-09-88, SERIES\n              OF 1988\n\nMemorandum Circular No. 04-09-88, dated 21 April 1988, provides for the necessary\nradio equipment on board vessel that will enhance safety life and property at sea.\n\nThe above-mentioned Circular is hereby amended to delete the Telegraphy installation\nwith capability on 500 KHz for liners and cargo vessels with 350 G.T. and above and\nmore than five (5) hours of navigation and replace with an auto watch receiver and\nautomatic tone generating device for 2182 KHz (for compliance within ninety days (90).\n\nThis Circular shall take effect immediately and amends above-mentioned circular and\nany other existing Circulars, Orders or Instructions or part thereof which is inconsistent\nherewith.\n\nJOSE LUIS A. ALCUAZ\n  COMMISSIONER\n\n                                            1",
    sections: [
      { heading: "Amended Equipment Requirement", body: "Deletes the requirement for 500 KHz telegraphy installation capability on liners and cargo vessels of 350 G.T. and above with more than five hours of navigation, replacing it with an auto watch receiver and automatic tone generating device for 2182 KHz, to be complied with within 90 days. Effective immediately, amending MC 04-09-88 and any inconsistent circulars." }
    ]
